---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import { planets } from "../data/planets";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Snapchat Emojis and Symbols: Complete Meaning Guide"
  description="Complete guide to Snapchat friendship emojis and symbols. Learn what Yellow Heart, Red Heart, Pink Hearts, Fire, and all Snapchat symbols mean."
  canonicalPath="/emojis-and-symbols"
>
  <section class="section">
    <Breadcrumb
      items={[
        { label: "Home", href: "/" },
        { label: "Emojis & Symbols" },
      ]}
    />

    <h1>Snapchat Emojis and Symbols: Complete Meaning Guide</h1>

    <div class="prose page-content">
      <p>
        Snapchat uses a rich system of friendship emojis and symbols to communicate relationship
        status between users. Unlike <strong>Snapchat Planets</strong> — which are exclusive to
        <strong>Snapchat Plus</strong> subscribers and visualize your top eight friends as a solar
        system — friendship emojis are visible to everyone and appear directly next to friend names
        in your chat list. This guide explains every major emoji and symbol on Snapchat, how they
        relate to the <a href="/snapchat-planets">Best Friends Solar System</a>, and what each one
        means for your friendships. Return to the <a href="/">Snapchat Planets homepage</a> for
        the interactive planet finder tool.
      </p>

      <h2>Friendship Emojis</h2>

      <h3>Yellow Heart 💛</h3>
      <p>
        The Yellow Heart appears when you and a friend are each other's #1 best friend on Snapchat.
        This is the most sought-after friendship emoji, equivalent to being each other's Mercury in
        the planetary system. Both users must snap each other more than anyone else for this emoji
        to appear. After two weeks, it upgrades to the Red Heart.
      </p>

      <h3>Red Heart ❤️</h3>
      <p>
        The Red Heart replaces the Yellow Heart after you and a friend maintain mutual #1 best
        friend status for two consecutive weeks. It signals a deepening bond and consistent daily
        interaction. Losing the Red Heart means someone else has become your top best friend.
      </p>

      <h3>Pink Hearts 💕</h3>
      <p>
        Pink Hearts appear after two months of mutual #1 best friend status. This is the longest-lasting
        friendship emoji and represents one of Snapchat's most enduring digital bonds. Pink Hearts
        indicate remarkable consistency in daily snapping habits.
      </p>

      <h3>Fire 🔥</h3>
      <p>
        The Fire emoji marks an active snap streak — consecutive days of exchanging snaps with a
        friend within 24-hour windows. Streak length is displayed as a number next to the fire. Long
        streaks contribute to higher planet rankings in the Best Friends Solar System.
      </p>

      <h3>100 💯</h3>
      <p>
        The 100 emoji celebrates reaching a 100-day snap streak with a friend. It replaces the
        standard Fire emoji temporarily to mark this milestone achievement.
      </p>

      <h3>Sunglasses 😎</h3>
      <p>
        Sunglasses appear when you and a friend share a mutual best friend — someone who is a top
        best friend for both of you. It indicates overlapping social circles and shared close
        connections.
      </p>

      <h2>Planet Heart Emojis</h2>
      <p>
        Each planet in the Snapchat solar system also displays specific heart emojis alongside
        friend names. These planet-specific hearts differ from the mutual best friend emojis above
        and are only visible within the Snapchat Plus solar system view:
      </p>
      <ul>
        {
          planets.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/snapchat-planets/${p.slug}`}>{p.name}</a> (Rank #{p.rank}): {p.hearts}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <h2>Emojis vs Planets: Key Differences</h2>
      <p>
        Friendship emojis are mutual and visible to both friends involved. Snapchat Planets are a
        one-directional view — only the Snapchat Plus subscriber sees the solar system ranking.
        Emojis reflect mutual top-friend status, while planets rank all eight of your most-interacted
        friends regardless of whether the ranking is mutual. You can be someone's Mercury while they
        are your Neptune, but you cannot have Yellow Hearts unless you are mutually each other's #1.
      </p>

      <p>
        For the complete planets order and interactive finder tool, visit our
        <a href="/">Snapchat Planets homepage</a> or explore the
        <a href="/snapchat-planets">Snapchat Planets hub page</a> for individual planet guides
        covering Mercury through Neptune.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .page-content {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }
</style>
